From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TB351FU <dev@tb351fu>
Date: Thu Jul 9 00:00:00 2026
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Disable framework-res.apk binary patcher in build.sh

The binary XML patcher for framework-res.apk invalidates APK
Signature Scheme v2/v3, causing the package manager to reject
the APK.  The runtime fix in ParsedPermissionUtils (patch 0001)
makes this patcher unnecessary.

---
 build.sh | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build.sh b/build.sh
index 0000000..0000000
--- a/build.sh
+++ b/build.sh
@@ -28,8 +28,14 @@ export SKIP_ABI_CHECKS=true
 #make bacon | tee log.txt
 make systemimage productimage systemextimage vendorimage
-#make framework-res -j$(nproc)
-#make systemimage
-
-# Post-build: patch framework-res.apk
-python3 device/lenovo/tb351fu/patches/patch_framework_res.py \
-  --apk out/target/product/tb351fu/system/framework/framework-res.apk
-#make systemimage
+
+# ── Post-build: patch framework-res.apk (DISABLED) ──────────────────────────
+# The runtime fix in ParsedPermissionUtils.declareDuplicatePermission() skips
+# the duplicate permission check for the android package, making the binary
+# XML patcher unnecessary.  The patcher also breaks APK v2/v3 signing.
+# See lineage.md section #4 for details.
+# python3 device/lenovo/tb351fu/patches/patch_framework_res.py \
+#   --apk out/target/product/tb351fu/system/framework/framework-res.apk
+# make systemimage
